  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Landen Roupp couldn't make it out of the fifth, and San Diego's four-run second buried them.",
    "what_this_means": "They had chances and converted two of them. Runners scoring in the fourth kept it within reach. But San Diego's early surge and the short starter's quick exit made this a slow bleed rather than a sudden collapse. Jung Hoo Lee went 2-for-3, the lineup managed seven hits, but the damage was done before they could build anything real. Sam Hentges and Dylan Smith held the line after Roupp left, combining for 2.1 scoreless innings with three strikeouts, but the bullpen was managing a game that was already decided. Eight strikeouts against seven hits tells the whole story: contact failures and no depth to the order. The inconsistency that defined the season showed up again in the second inning, and they never recovered from that hole.",
    "what_to_watch": "Texas sends TBD to the mound tonight at 5:05 PT. Webb gets the ball for the Giants, and he'll need the lineup to find something earlier than it did in San Diego.",
